{"id":"b6692a4d165078af460ab0079c634d45b5e4e7eb","axis":"silent","repo":"astral-sh/ruff","sha":"b6692a4d165078af460ab0079c634d45b5e4e7eb","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"crates/ty_server/src/lib.rs","lines":["@@ -1,3 +1,82 @@","+//! The ty language server.","+//!","+//! ## Request handling","+//!","+//! The main loop communicates with the editor and delegates code analysis to background","+//! workers. When the user hovers over a name, for example, a worker looks up its type","+//! while the main loop stays free to handle the user's next edit. When the worker","+//! returns the result, the main loop forwards it to the editor.","+//!","+//! ```text","+//!           buffered stdin","+//! [Editor] --------------> [Reader]","+//!    ^                        |","+//!    |                 [[ Input | 0 ]]","+//!    |                        |","+//!    |                        v","+//!    |                   [Main loop] -----------------------> [[ Jobs | 2048 ]]","+//!    |                      |    ^                                    |","+//!    |                      |    |                                    v","+//!    |                      |    +-- [[ Actions | unbounded ]] <- [Workers]","+//!    |                      |                                         |","+//!    |                      v                                         |","+//!    |               [[ Writer | 0 ]] <--- progress notifications ----+","+//!    |                      |","+//!    |                      v","+//!    +------------------ [Writer]","+//!       buffered stdout","+//! ```","+//!","+//! **Legend**","+//!","+//! - `[ ]` An active component or thread.","+//! - `[[ name | capacity ]]` A channel. `0` means a direct handoff, `2048` allows","+//!   2,048 waiting jobs per pool, and `unbounded` means no fixed limit.","+//! - `-->` Direction of message flow.","+//! - `buffered stdin` and `buffered stdout` OS pipes that buffer bytes.","+//!","+//! ## Back pressure","+//!","+//! The `Jobs` queue lets a hover request wait for a worker while the main loop handles","+//! other messages. If the queue is already full, the main loop replies with","+//! `RequestFailed` and the editor can drop the request or retry it later. Waiting for","+//! space would prevent the main loop from forwarding completed responses or handling","+//! `shutdown`.","+//!","+//! The `Actions` queue is unbounded so workers can return results even when the main","+//! loop is waiting for them. For example, applying an edit can require the main loop to","+//! wait for queued jobs to release their database snapshots. If all workers were blocked","+//! trying to return results, those queued jobs could never run. In practice, most jobs","+//! produce a single response. When responses accumulate, the main loop drains ready","+//! actions before reading more requests from the editor.","+//!","+//! The zero-capacity `Input` and `Writer` channels let back pressure reach the OS pipes.","+//! If the main loop falls behind, the reader waits and the editor's writes block once","+//! stdin fills. If the editor stops reading, stdout can fill and the writer must finish","+//! its current write before it can accept another response.","+//!","+//! ## Request cancellation","+//!","+//! The main loop queues a hover request in `Jobs`. If the editor cancels the request","+//! while it is pending, the main loop marks it cancelled and replies immediately with","+//! a cancellation error so the editor doesn't have to wait for a worker.","+//!","+//! - If the job is still queued, it stays in `Jobs` until a worker picks it up. The","+//!   worker checks for cancellation at that point and skips the request.","+//! - If a worker has already started processing the request, it returns the result","+//!   through `Actions`. Before forwarding the result, the main loop checks","+//!   whether the request is still pending. It discards the result because it already","+//!   sent the editor a cancellation response.","+//!","+//! ## Salsa cancellation","+//!","+//! Applying an edit can cause Salsa to interrupt a worker analyzing an older database","+//! snapshot. The editor may still need the result, so some requests, such as code","+//! completion, support a retry. The worker sends the request back through `Actions`,","+//! and the main loop automatically retries it with a fresh snapshot. If `Jobs` is full","+//! or shutdown has started, the main loop replies with the request's cancellation error","+//! (`ContentModified` for completions).","+"," use std::{num::NonZeroUsize, sync::Arc};"," "," use anyhow::Context;"],"additions":79,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"crates/ty_server/src/server.rs","lines":["@@ -33,6 +33,13 @@ pub(crate) use main_loop::{"," pub(crate) use script_progress::ScriptProgress;"," pub(crate) type Result<T> = std::result::Result<T, api::Error>;"," ","+/// Maximum number of requests waiting for a worker.","+///","+/// The exact number is arbitrary. A high limit leaves room for bursts of editor","+/// requests. When the queue fills, the server rejects new background requests","+/// to apply back pressure.","+pub(crate) const MAX_QUEUED_REQUESTS: usize = 2048;","+"," pub struct Server {","     connection: Connection,","     worker_threads: NonZeroUsize,","@@ -109,9 +116,9 @@ impl Server {","             }),","         )?;"," ","-        // The number 32 was chosen arbitrarily. The main goal was to have enough capacity to queue","-        // some responses before blocking.","-        let (main_loop_sender, main_loop_receiver) = crossbeam::channel::bounded(32);","+        // An edit can wait for database snapshots held by queued jobs. Workers must be","+        // able to return their results while the main loop waits for those snapshots.","+        let (main_loop_sender, main_loop_receiver) = crossbeam::channel::unbounded();","         let client = Client::new(main_loop_sender.clone(), connection.sender.clone());"," ","         let unknown_options = &initializ